ight perhaps. Use overlay low alpha.\n- Wood countertop: horizontal planks with grain curves (sin lines) semi-transparent; draw many wavy lines using points.\n- Tiles: backsplash pale zellige tiles behind counter maybe y=560..740; but window & cabinets. Create subtle square grid with slight color variance. This adds detail.\n- Window outside: layered gradient sky, sun disc, silhouettes of trees and rooftops, maybe hills. Blur slightly through glass. Muntins.\n\nComposition details in unit coordinates 1600x1200:\n\nBackground wall 0..1600, 0..900? Floor below y=960. Actually lower cabinets/counter hide floor until bottom? We can show floor at bottom around island? Straight-on view: bottom y>1050 could be floor with rug? If standard eye-level, counters at y=750, lower cabinets to 1050, floor visible 1050..1200. That's fine. Add a wooden stool and cat maybe in bottom right. But flat straight-on composition, floor strip adds depth.\n\nLet's set:\n- Wall from y=0..1050, color warm buttery plaster.\n- Backsplash y=620..780? Countertop y=780..845; lower cabinets y=845..1080; floor y=1080..1200.\n- Window x=545..1055, y=130..650, frame.\n- Sink centered x=650..950, basin top at 790. Faucet from y=650..780. Window sill at y=650? Hmm sink below window; window bottom 580 maybe, backsplash 580..780. Set window y=100..590. Frame. Window sill at 590..620. Wall/backsplash below.\n- Counter at y=775..850.\n- Sink basin carved into counter at x=680..920, y=790..850 front apron; if farmhouse sink, white apron front extends below counter to 930. We can draw white basin top oval and apron front.\n- Lower cabinets on either side from y=850..1070, sage green shaker doors; sink cabinet white apron in center? Farmhouse sink sits in sink base, apron visible at y=850..930; below may be cabinet door. Fine.\n- Upper left open shelves x=120..460 y=180..500, 2 shelves with plates, crocks, plant. Upper right maybe glass-front cabinet or open shelves x=1140..1480, y=170..500 with copper pots, jars