th alpha 80, or draw 2-3 translucent circles, but ensure no hard edges. Currently 3 hard-edged circles sizes 190/110/48, all visible as disks; use blurred layer.\n- Remove huge vertical reflectionsthat look like strange light. Keep subtle.\n- Curtains: current blocky columns with sharp edges and no proper flow. Improve by giving wavy inner edge and tieback, softer folds. Maybe reduce width to 70 and make them more natural. Or remove curtains entirely for cleaner window. Cozy kitchen can have simple linen cafe curtains half-height; but current ones hide too much and look like cardboard. Let's improve: curtains should be at very outer edges, x 500..555 and 1045..1100, narrower; draw folds with 2px, no stiff dark stripes. Add soft shadow. And more translucent? Let's do side curtains with top width ~75, mid 60, bottom 55, tieback at y=400. Curved outer/inner edges. Use gradient fill? Need shape gradient clipped, or fill solid + fold lines. Rounded top.\n\n- Curtain rod currently starts x=482 y=66, spans; okay.\n- Dark edge bars on wall remove.\n- Cabinet layout: looks like a flat wall of cabinets, okay but the left/right countertop has weird black vertical edges at x=56. Countertop right end is at 1544, close to edge; okay.\n- Sink: tiny faucet but okay. Farmhouse sink looks drawn. Need more depth maybe.\n- Cat looks like a weird croissant, but cute; improve ears? It looks like a loaf with face. Could keep. Stool legs too thin but okay.\n- Rug is flat ellipse with concentric rings and little pattern; okay but too dominant? It is cozy.\n- Floor slippers look like two pink blobs; could improve.\n- Major issue: cabinets are all at same flat frontal view, image very symmetrical and static. Could add asymmetry, more depth, shadows. But user just wants cozy kitchen in morning; current already conveys. Still, we can significantly improve style.\n\nNeed decide effort. We have lots of tokens. Aim better.\n\nPotential enhancements:\n1. Fix vertical bands.\n2. Improve curtains naturalness and remove shadow band. Add soft folds and maybe only one curtain partly visible.\n3. Improve window outside with more depth: gradient sky, soft sun glow, layered trees, a branch with leaves maybe, warm haze. Add thin mullions.\n4. Add warmer directional light and stronger contrast; image currently washed out. Increase shadows, warm highlights. Cabinets more saturated and shaded.\n5. Add more 3D depth to countertop: perspective front edge, undercounter shadow. It's there but too flat. Could darken backsplash shadow.\n6. Add upper left/right shadows and highlights.\n7. Improve knife board and objects scale maybe. The kettle is huge and looks like a glass box with a handle; because body rrect and outline, floral details look odd. Could make kettle more rounded (use rounded rect with larger radius, elliptical body?) It currently looks like a glass toaster. A stovetop kettle should have a curved body with spout. Improve with a more rounded silhouette using custom polygon/ellipse.\n8. Coffee mug looks okay.\n9. Right side objects small but fine.\n10. Pendant lamp is flat but okay.\n11. Hanging herbs left are hidden by curtain? Little green thing at x=460 between shelf and curtain; okay.\n12. The big radial vignette has dark corners? The image edges dark not too much.\n13. Wall bands: fix.\n\nNeed maybe create a more painterly version with textured shading. We can add:\n- Soft shadow under shelf/cabinet.\n- Warm glow around window edges.\n- Some careful highlights.\n\nLet's inspect crops of left and right to identify issues."}
