~966,y~650) a diagonal boundary to (1050,380) (orig 1600,y~780). Another parallel from (0,690) to (900,800)? It might be the broad light beam `beam` polygon with alpha 16, but because `ImageDraw` on RGBA with alpha and alpha_composite should lighten. But the polygon fill is yellow, not dark. Hmm maybe the beam image has black edges due to antialias? We blurred, should not.\n\nActually the counter has large diagonal tonal regions because we drew `grad_rect` counter and then the light beam? No, the beam is composited over entire image; yellow alpha would warm.\n\nLook at the cabinet top rail: there's a dark diagonal from x~1000 y~800 to 1600, maybe underlying? No.\n\nLet's trace code near counter:\n- grad_rect counter 56,748..1544,808.\n- planks horizontal, grain.\n- front edge.\n- warm sun poly (1000,750),(1530,750),(1544,830),(930,830) alpha 46.\n- cabinets from 828.\n- sink.\n- objects.\n- light rays broad beam.\n\nThe triangle on backsplash in crop begins at y~650 and extends into counter. Backsplash is 626..755, so yes. The dark bands could be leftover from `soft_shadow` of upper shelf? no. Wait the \"curtain shadow\" polygon drawn earlier covers x 540..620, not right.\n\nWhat about `shadow_poly(im, [(570,90),(620,300),(600,590),(540,600),(560,300)], 18, 22)` - left only.\nSoft shadows from right shelf at 1130..1490 y 306..326 and 500..518, not diagonal.\nShadow of hanging copper pans? copper_pan uses `soft_shadow` at each pan bottom, small ellipses.\nShadow of fruit bowl etc small.\nCould the diagonal bands be `beam` polygon rendered dark due to alpha_composite with RGBA? No.\n\nWait, the broad beam is drawn after objects. Its polygon `[(552,122),(1048,122),(1560,900),(930,1200),(640,1200),(520,760)]` covers huge area. The fill is (255,219,147,16), should lighten. But there may be an issue with `Image.alpha_composite`: compositing a translucent light color should lighten. The result's diagonal edges correspond to beam boundaries, appearing as *lighter* bands? In