{"type":"thinking","text":"Great. Need also layer draws `bd`, `spd`, `md`, `fd`, etc. unaffected.\n\nImplement BlendDraw class after helper defs, replace `d = ImageDraw.Draw(im)` with proxy. The proxy must implement methods. We can also let internal draw use the same `im`. Important: `ell`, `rrect`, `rect`, `poly`, `line` helpers call d methods; they pass already scaled coords and width (int). The proxy methods receive boxes in scaled pixel coords. Bbox calculations straightforward.\n\nNeed careful with RGBA color detection. In `rgba`, returns 4-tuple; all fills. For line `fill` maybe 4-tuple. `width` maybe scaled int. For `arc`, `fill` is 4-tuple and `width` scaled. For polygon, `outline` may be 4-tuple; `width` scaled.\n\nImplementation:\n```\nclass BlendDraw:\n  def __init__(self, im):\n    self.im=im; self.base=ImageDraw.Draw(im)\n    self.scratch=Image.new('RGBA', im.size, (0,0,0,0))\n    self.sd=ImageDraw.Draw(self.scratch)\n  def _alpha(self,c): return isinstance(c,tuple) and len(c)==4 and c[3]<255\n  def _run(self, method, bbox, args, kwargs):\n    if not (alpha(fill) or alpha(outline)):\n       getattr(self.base, method)(...); return\n    x0,y0,x1,y1 = bbox with margin\n    clamp to im\n    self.scratch.paste((0,0,0,0), (x0,y0,x1,y1))\n    getattr(self.sd, method)(...)\n    tile=self.scratch.crop((x0,y0,x1,y1))\n    self.im.alpha_composite(tile, (x0,y0))\n    # optional clear\n```\nFor scratch, drawing at absolute coords is fine. Need clear after? If we clear before each call at bbox, old content outside bbox irrelevant. But if a previous shape's bbox overlaps new one and wasn't cleared, it may leak. Clear after compositing too to be safe; or clear only before. Since we clear bbox before each, previous shape inside same bbox cleared. If previous shape extends outside bbox but its pixels are outside, crop excludes. Fine. Clear before is enough.\n- But `scratch` starts transparent.\n- For line joints, bbox margin width+2.\n- For `arc`, bbox plus width.\n- For