{"type":"thinking","text":"Before that, add light enhancements.\n\nLet's inspect sky palette and add peach. Current grad top #bcd8e2 to #ffe1ac. Change to #b7d7e0 -> #ffd59a, and maybe add a radial warm glow around sun. The sun at 600,192; horizon at 574. Add `glow(im, 620, 220, 240, 210, (255,214,140), 130, 30)` before trees, and a small bright core. But with alpha compositing on layers, glow will lighten sky. Good.\n- Trees currently muted green; make them richer and slightly warmer with sunlit highlights. Add a few warm edges on tree circles on left side.\n- Meadow #c6c690; make it warmer #d9c17f with green tufts. Fine.\n\nWindow glass reflection: after alpha fix, white strips? There are none visible now? The reflection polygons alpha 13 are barely visible. That's fine.\n- Add a soft diagonal reflection highlight across the glass, alpha 20, blurred, maybe not needed.\n\nCurtains: pale cream, low contrast, okay but stiff. Could add shadows behind curtains on wall to make them pop: `soft_shadow` around each panel, but that may look good. Draw a soft shadow to the right of each curtain on wall (not inside window?) Since curtains overlap window, shadow on wall only. Hard to clip. Could add a soft shading strip along inner edge of curtain itself; already. In the image, curtains look like flat boards with a jagged inner edge. Add **vertical fold shadows** stronger (alpha 45) and rounded bottom hem. They currently have fold lines but barely visible. Make folds more visible with darker #d3b387 alpha 50 and highlights. Also add a soft shadow at the top under the rod.\n- Their inner edges are wavy but look like zigzag. Smooth them: use more points, but okay.\n- Maybe tiebacks are too high; at y=390, mid-window. Fine.\n\nCould replace curtains with **cafe curtains** only at top? That would show more window and avoid stiff columns. But side curtains add coziness. Improve folds.\n\nLet's implement light first. Use `glow` after sky before trees; change sky colors; stronger outside contrast. Also add sun patch and warm right side.\n\nCode around sky. Replace:\n```\ngrad_rect(... '#bcd8e2', '#ffe1ac')\nglow(... 95)\nell sun ...\n```\nwith:\n```\ngrad_rect(... '#b3d4df', '#ffd49b')\nglow(im, 616, 210, 230, 200, (255,219,146), 135, 32)\nell(d,(584,176,614,206), fill=(255,250,220,120))\n```\nBut `ell` with alpha 120 uses proxy and will blend. Good. Add a second brighter core smaller alpha 180.\n- `glow` alpha 135 maybe intense. Use 110.\n\nAfter all drawing, increase sunpatch alpha from 18 to 38 and add a golden soft patch on right cabinets:\n```\nsuncab = layer, polygon [(1150,840),(1500,840),(1544,1050),(1200,1050)] fill (255,205,130,20), blur 40\n```\nThis would lighten cabinets on right, but the cat/stool also there. Subtle.\nAdd **warm glow** on right side:\n`glow(im, 1280, 900, 420, 360, (255,200,120), 30, 90)` after sunpatch. This may wash the cat; maybe before objects? Too late. Use 18.\n- Add golden light on floor right `poly` existing? There is a long light on floor with alpha 48 drawn early (hard polygon). With correct alpha compositing, it may now look stronger; in current image floor is relatively uniform. Add a soft floor patch behind stool with `sunpatch` layer blur.\n\nMaybe enough: warmer sky + sun patch + vignette. The image is pastel, not necessarily needs strong light.\n\nLet's modify sky and sunpatch, plus add warm glow after light."}
